…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd David called for Zadok and Abiathar the priests, and for the Levites, for Uriel, Asaiah, and Joel, Shemaiah, and Eliel, and Amminadab,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖand said unto them, Ye are the chief of the fathers of the Levites: sanctify yourselves, both ye and your brethren, that ye may bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel unto the place that I have prepared for it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor because ye did it not at the first, the LORD our God made a breach upon us, for that we sought him not after the due order.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcSo the priests and the Levites sanctified themselves to bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—And the children of the Levites bare the ark of God upon their shoulders with the staves thereon, as Moses commanded according to the word of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁAnd David spake to the chief of the Levites to appoint their brethren to be the singers with instruments of musick, psalteries and harps and cymbals, sounding, by lifting up the voice with joy.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; and of his brethren, Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari their brethren, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙìand with them their brethren of the second degree, Zechariah, Ben, and Jaaziel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Unni, Eliab, and Benaiah, and Maaseiah, and Mattithiah, and Elipheleh, and Mikneiah, and Obed-edom, and Jeiel, the porters.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWSo the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, were appointed to sound with cymbals of brass;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚and Zechariah, and Aziel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Unni, and Eliab, and Maaseiah, and Benaiah, with psalteries on Alamoth;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyand Mattithiah, and Elipheleh, and Mikneiah, and Obed-edom, and Jeiel, and Azaziah, with harps on the Sheminith to excel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhAnd Chenaniah, chief of the Levites, was for song: he instructed about the song, because he was skilful.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ7And Berechiah and Elkanah were doorkeepers for the ark.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÙAnd Shebaniah, and Jehoshaphat, and Nethaneel, and Amasai, and Zechariah, and Benaiah, and Eliezer, the priests, did blow with the trumpets before the ark of God: and Obed-edom and Jehiah were doorkeepers for the ark.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡So David, and the elders of Israel, and the captains over thousands, went to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the house of Obed-edom with joy.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd it came to pass, when God helped the Levites that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD, that they offered seven bullocks and seven rams.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊAnd David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, and all the Levites that bare the ark, and the singers, and Chenaniah the master of the song with the singers: David also had upon him an ephod of linen.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºThus all Israel brought up the ark of the covenant of the LORD with shouting, and with sound of the cornet, and with trumpets, and with cymbals, making a noise with psalteries and harps.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖAnd it came to pass, as the ark of the covenant of the LORD came to the city of David, that Michal the daughter of Saul looking out at a window saw king David dancing and playing: and she despised him in her heart.¦layout ªlast_verse